 "note": "The routes the dispatcher tries, in this order, for a free drone pilot. Apophis keeps this file: put a route that pays first, a test with `max_ships` before it enters for all, and end with `park`. Set on 2026-11-15 by the Fleet Admiral at the handover: the missions that pay once, then what paid, then park. No route that loses money stands here to fill time (orders F8). 2026-11-15 21:40 UTC (Apophis): voidborn-first-steps out, Acubens Belt read 0 carbon ore at 21:01 UTC (requests.log ENT-039); hunt-gsc-veil-ray takes only the railgun ship for turn T5. 2026-11-15 22:05 UTC (Apophis): voidborn-concurrent at the head, once per pilot, buys nothing, +3,000 cr (Mercury's test, queue.log ENT-038; orders F8). census-frontier before park since orders.log ENT-006. 2026-11-15 23:28 UTC (Apophis, turn T7, orders.log ENT-007): the railgun test ended (no gain measured, the ammunition ran out), both home veil-ray herds take every pulse drone again; the five frontier veil-ray herds and Ruchbah again, each a test with one ship, `alone` and an empty hold; five yield tests of species no run of ours has looted, in policed space; no hunt takes a ship with a Piercing Railgun I until it carries ammunition. 2026-11-15 23:38 UTC (Apophis): voidborn-precedence (4,000 cr once, +3,896 in 15 min) and voidborn-selling (1,000 cr once for the pilots that hold the starter mission, +865 in 5 min) at the head: their first RESULT lines are read (data/routes/runs.jsonl, 23:20 to 23:32 UTC; orders F8, missions that pay once first). 2026-11-15 23:40 UTC (Apophis): voidborn-first-hunt-nexus at the head (its first RESULT line, 23:20 UTC: +974 cr, one-time 1,000, 18.9 minutes); hunt-test-siphon-bell-jelly out: two kills dropped crystallized biogas and a levity bladder, both bid 1 to 2 cr. 2026-11-15 23:51 UTC (Apophis): voidborn-first-hunt-gsc and -acubens beside -nexus (first RESULT lines of 23:20 UTC: +934 cr in 25.9 min and +945 cr in 28.0 min, one-time 1,000 each): three herds, one hunter each. 2026-11-15 23:57 UTC (Apophis): voidborn-first-hunt-schedar, a fourth herd for First Hunt beyond the border (a test, one ship, empty hold, alone); the node-gamma ice-belt and frozen-drift yield tests out: their drops have no bid over 2 cr. 2026-11-16 00:07 UTC (Apophis): hunt-test-eltanin-kiln-snail out: 0 kills, the drone driven from 75 to 46 hull. 2026-11-16 03:00 UTC (Apophis, orders.log ENT-011): First Hunt on three more herds beyond the border, each one jump from The Experiment (Ironhollow Echo Ejecta 26 and Fading Signal 19 belt-grazers, Achernar Belt 12; 21 drones still wait for the mission); voidborn-first-hunt-schedar out (a foreign pilot at the place in 8 of its 9 runs, data/routes/logs/); hunt-garnet-dim-lattice-veil-ray out (6 runs at a loss, -600 cr per ship-hour) and hunt-test-acubens-patina-grazer out (5 runs at a loss, -560), orders F8; mission-cracking-the-shell-central and voidborn-first-steps in (once per pilot, measured 1,410 and 640 cr a run); two veil-ray herds of the route maker as tests (Dimming Pocket, Denebola); five yield tests, one ship each, of species no run of ours has looted, herds of ten or more and 100 hull or less (cinder-sylph, patina-grazer, slag-tortoise, glitterback crab, hollow-pilgrim). The veil-ray hunts in the order of their measured credits per ship-hour. 2026-11-16 03:13 UTC (Apophis): mission-cracking-the-shell-achernar before -central (the mission asks pressblisters at any ice field; Node Gamma Ice Belt read 0 of them at 02:27 and 03:04 UTC, Achernar Frost Ring 8 at 01:21 UTC); voidborn-first-hunt-schedar back, last before the census: the fill gate counts it paying with its reward (+50 cr a run over 9 runs). 2026-11-16 03:16 UTC (Apophis): the cinder-sylph test paid (+894 cr in 12.2 min, 2 ember glands at 480 cr): it heads the hunts; two more cinder-sylph herds as tests (Lesath, GSC-0050). 2026-11-16 03:25 UTC (Apophis): both Cracking the Shell routes out: in 19 runs of the fleet every pilot with First Hunt booked was offered the mission (7 of 7) and every pilot without it was not (12 of 12, 'not offered'), and such a run counts as done for the pilot (dispatch.done_once); back when a route can require a booked reward (owed by Unity) or a refused accept is no try. 2026-11-16 05:16 UTC (Apophis, turn T10, orders.log ENT-012): voidborn-conductive-lattice second (+10,893 cr once per pilot, EVERY ADMIRAL; its limits are Mercury's); mission-cracking-the-shell-achernar back after First Hunt with `requires.booked`; hunt-test-lesath-cinder-sylph up among the paying hunts (first RESULT 03:40 UTC: 1 kill, 2 ember glands, +1,456 cr in 17.2 min); census-guard-ice before census-frontier (the guard of block APOPHIS (2)). Out (orders F8): voidborn-first-hunt-ironhollow-echo, voidborn-first-hunt-ironhollow-fading, hunt-dimming-pocket-veil-ray, hunt-denebola-fractured-prism-veil-ray, hunt-test-gsc-0050-cinder-sylph, hunt-test-atlas-patina-grazer, hunt-test-garnet-slag-tortoise, hunt-test-goldcrest-glitterback-crab, hunt-test-tanglewood-hollow-pilgrim: no drop that sells (patina-grazer: carapace and meat; hollow-pilgrim: crystal melt bid 54 cr), no kill in two runs (GSC-0050, Garnet slag-tortoise, Goldcrest crab), a ship not ours at the place in two runs in a row (Dimming Pocket, Denebola), First Hunt at Ironhollow not offered and closed by the loss stop (data/routes/runs.jsonl). 2026-11-16 05:17 UTC (Apophis): mission-cracking-the-shell-central after the Achernar one, its hunt now at Alnair Ice Fields (Node Gamma Ice Belt holds no pressblister since 01:50 UTC); the Achernar one rests under the loss stop on its two refused runs of 03:13 to 03:22 UTC until the six-hour window moves on. 2026-11-16 05:20 UTC (fill.py, Apophis): voidborn-first-hunt-acubens taken out. 2026-11-16 09:02 UTC (fill.py, Apophis): voidborn-signal-fragments added. 2026-11-16 09:02 UTC (fill.py, Apophis): voidborn-network-expansion added. 2026-11-16 09:05 UTC (Apophis): the seven veil-ray hunts taken out: the verdigris curd bid (330 cr x 50) left every station of our books between 07:08 and 07:51 UTC (data/market/history.jsonl) and has not come back; their 21 runs since 07:05 UTC made -1,851 cr (data/routes/runs.jsonl). voidborn-first-hunt-achernar and -schedar taken out: a ship not ours at the place in every run since 06:49 UTC, 16 runs, 0 hand-ins, -1,221 cr. 2026-11-16 09:19 UTC (Apophis): mission-cracking-the-shell-central taken out: alnair_ice_fields read no pressblister at 09:07 UTC (data/wildlife/alnair.json); 5 runs of the fleet from 05:43 UTC, 0 hand-ins, -871 cr. Its move is asked of Unity (five plans fly it). 2026-11-16 13:09 UTC (Apophis, orders.log ENT-014): the once line of the Central Nexus board at the head after Signal Fragments (voidborn-first-steps-board, -network-expansion, -collective-provides, -signal-protocol; Trade's files and limits); voidborn-first-steps out (off); the seven veil-ray hunts back, each behind the curd bid of its sell station (requires.bid), in the order of their measured credits per ship-hour; voidborn-first-hunt-achernar back and mission-cracking-the-shell-achernar with a herd floor of three; mission-cracking-the-shell-central (Unity's, now at GSC-0041 with a floor of three) back after it. 2026-11-16 13:16 UTC (Apophis): train-navigation-home, a test with one ship before the census: what navigation XP a jump gives toward Signal Fragments. 2026-11-16 13:21 UTC (Apophis): sell-curd-central-nexus, sell-curd-node-beta, sell-curd-experiment before the hunts, one ship each as tests: the curd the veil-ray hunts stored while its bid was gone is sold where it lies. 2026-11-16 13:29 UTC (fill.py, Apophis): added mission-ghosts-in-the-cloud-node, open to ships that waited. 2026-11-16 13:31 UTC (fill.py, Apophis): added voidborn-first-hunt-acubens, open to ships that waited. 2026-11-16 15:10 UTC (Unity, a stopgap on Suggi's word that no ship is idle): gather-gsc-0027-prism-scatter, gather-hamal-crystal-bloom added before the census as standing work for the ships that wait; its Admiral replaces them with its own standing work at its next turn (the skill fleet-play, `Plan a Division`). 2026-11-16 15:31 UTC (fill.py, Unity): added voidborn-first-hunt-intercrus-belt, open to ships that waited.",
